    "task_id": "lane-runtime-reload-gate",
    "goal": "When an integrated child changed the plugin build, the next Lane admission pauses with `runtime_reload_required` instead of running a stale runtime, and a confirmed resume admits it, recording `runtime_skew_acknowledged` when the build still differs (Spec branch-boundary-r2-followups D9).",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "AC1",
        "assertion": "In a plugin-source repository, after a child integrates a commit that changes `plugins/immune-brain/dist/claude/mcp-server.mjs` so the Parent tip bundle differs from the loaded build, the next admission or redo creates no Lane, the batch pauses `needs_human` with `runtime_reload_required` naming the integrated commit, and in-flight children keep running; with an equal build, or in a repository that is not the plugin source, admission proceeds without a pause.",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v2\",\n  \"command\": {\n    \"executable\": \"bun\",\n    \"argv\": [\n      \"test\",\n      \"tests/batch-runtime-reload-gate.test.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"cwd\": \".\",\n    \"timeout_ms\": 300000,\n    \"max_output_bytes\": 131072\n  },\n  \"environment\": {\n    \"prepare\": null,\n    \"writable_paths\": []\n  }\n}\n"
